Pass STRATOCLAVE_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL into the backend's task definition

THE GAP. docs/DEPLOYMENT.md's "Post-deploy: first admin" says to export this variable and redeploy the ECS stack, and
backend/bootstrap/seed.py does read it at startup and write the generated password into Secrets Manager. The ECS stack
already pre-creates that secret with an empty placeholder and grants the task PutSecretValue on exactly its ARN. Every
part of the mechanism is present except the one that carries the value: the variable appears nowhere in iac/, so it
never reaches the container.

OBSERVED on a clean deployment under a fresh prefix: the documented procedure runs, the rollout reports COMPLETED, and
the user pool has zero users. Registering one task definition revision whose only difference is this variable produced
one CONFIRMED user and the {email, password} payload in the pre-created secret.

THE FIX follows the shape already used two lines above for ALLOW_ADMIN_CREATION, and is inert when unset: the backend
treats an empty string as "not set" and is additionally a no-op once any admin-role user exists.

Sent as a request to the project separately. Delete this patch once it is upstream -- tierbook-up detects that itself.
---
diff --git a/iac/bin/iac.ts b/iac/bin/iac.ts
index c919e46..2ac1996 100644
--- a/iac/bin/iac.ts
+++ b/iac/bin/iac.ts
@@ -125,6 +125,12 @@ const allowAdminCreation = process.env.ALLOW_ADMIN_CREATION || 'false';
 // operators control it via the CDK deploy path without touching SSM directly.
 const allowAdminCreationUntil = process.env.ALLOW_ADMIN_CREATION_UNTIL || '';
 
+// First-admin bootstrap. Read at backend STARTUP by bootstrap/seed.py, which is a no-op when it is unset and when an
+// admin-role user already exists, so passing it through unconditionally is safe and idempotent. The ECS stack already
+// pre-creates `<prefix>/bootstrap-admin-temp-password` and grants the task `PutSecretValue` on exactly that ARN for
+// this path; without the variable reaching the container, that secret and that grant have no writer.
+const bootstrapAdminEmail = process.env.STRATOCLAVE_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL || '';
+
 // Environment flag drives production-only knobs (deletion protection,
 // retain-on-delete tables, stricter cdk-nag rules).
 const envName = process.env.ENVIRONMENT || 'development';
@@ -547,6 +553,9 @@ const ecsStack = new EcsStack(app, stackName(prefix, 'ecs'), {
     ALLOW_ADMIN_CREATION: allowAdminCreation,
     ALLOW_ADMIN_CREATION_UNTIL: allowAdminCreationUntil,
 
+    // Empty string is treated as unset by the backend, so this is inert until an operator sets it.
+    STRATOCLAVE_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL: bootstrapAdminEmail,
+
     // Tenant. The per-user token quota is a loose fairness backstop, not the
     // binding ceiling — that is the seat-scaled dollar pool a tenant now gets at
     // creation (docs/design/limits.md, C14). A hardcoded '100000' here would have
